[226.930327, "o", "  qwen3.8-flash-next — 9 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ One leftover to check: ensurepip created temp dirs during its runs. Verif…\r\n[approval] bash: ls -d /tmp/tmp* 2>&1; echo EXIT=$?\r\necho \"=== pip still healthy post-cleanup ===\"; python3 -m pip --version 2>&1; echo EXIT=$? — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls -d /tmp/tmp* 2>&1; echo EXIT=$? echo \"=== pip still healthy post-cl…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 10 tool call(s) so far\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ compute \r\n    ✓ compute 852 - 841 = 11\r\n  ⚙ note \r\n    ✓ note — ensurepip gotcha on this machine: `python3 -m ensurepip --up\r\n  [tools] 12 call(s) without changing a file — nudging to decide\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ task \r\n    ✓ task implementor — 12 tool call(s)\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 9 tool call(s) so far\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 10 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ todo \r\n    ✓ todo — 2/2 done\r\nFixed. Your pip wasn'"]
[226.930358, "o", "t misconfigured or blocked — it was **missing**.\r\n\r\n**Cause.** PATH resolves `/usr/local/bin/python3` → Python 3.13.1 (prefix `/usr/local`), and its `site-packages` held only `README.txt` and `pip-24.3.1.dist-info/` — the `pip/` package directory itself was gone. 841 of the 852 files in pip's RECORD were absent from disk. So every invocation died at the import, not at the network:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3: No module named pip\r\n```\r\n\r\nTwo things this ruled out, since they're the usual suspects and both were *wrong* here: PEP 668 (`EXTERNALLY-MANAGED` exists only on the shadowed `/usr/bin/python3.11`, not on the active prefix), and permissions (you're root, the directory was writable). The 91%-full disk was incidental.\r\n\r\n**Fix.** `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade` — it reinstalls from the bundled wheel already on disk, no network needed.\r\n\r\n**One trap worth knowing:** that command alone reported exit 0 while repairing nothing — `Requirement already satisfied: pip in /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site"]
[226.930363, "o", "-packages (24.3.1)`. The orphaned `dist-info` made pip look installed. The stale directory had to be moved aside first, and only then did ensurepip really say `Successfully installed pip-24.3.1`. A green exit code on that step is not proof of a repair.\r\n\r\n**Check that it works.** After the repair, RECORD matches disk again (852 entries, 0 missing), `pip`/`pip3`/`python3 -m pip` all print `pip 24.3.1 ... (python 3.13)`, and a real round trip succeeded: `pip install six` downloaded from PyPI, `import six` worked, then uninstall removed it cleanly. The stale `dist-info` backup and scratch files are deleted; `/usr/bin/python3.11` was not touched, and nothing was written into this repository (which contains only the `.gnomon/` harness surface — no Python code, which is why the diagnosis had to reach outside it).\r\n\r\nIf you later want packages that won't break this way, `python3 -m venv ~/.venv` is the sturdier habit — but the system prefix itself is healthy now.\r\n\r\n[result] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-"]
[226.930367, "o", "flash tools=10 surface=016d83f6af9a\r\n"]
